<title>EGYPT: Egypt seeks 32,000 head of imported sheep.</title>
<headline>Egypt seeks 32,000 head of imported sheep.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The public-sector Egyptian Meat, Poultry and Food Supply Company said on Tuesday it wanted to buy 32,000 head of imported sheep.</p>
<p>The deadline for bids is January 28.</p>
<p>A company statement did not name the delivery date but Egypt usually imports large quantities of sheep at this time of year in readiness for the Moslem feast of Eid al-Adha, which falls this year on about April 17.</p>
<p>Last year the company bought 22,000 head of Australian merino sheep for the feast.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
